# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover / IntelliJ IDEA
.idea/

# Coverage reports (generated by make coverage)
lcov.info
coverage.json
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Old status files in root (superseded by docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md)
/*_STATUS.md
/*_SUMMARY.md
/*_NOTES.md
/deep_context.md

# dogfood pre-release protocol artefacts (the protocol creates these)
.dogfood/
# pmat writes caches and a context index under .pmat/, alongside REAL CONFIG
# that predates them: project.toml (v0.1.3) and quality-gates.yaml (v0.1.0,
# it carries the complexity/SATD thresholds the pre-commit gate enforces).
#
# So enumerate the ARTIFACTS rather than ignoring the directory and re-including
# configs. A blanket `.pmat/*` + `!` list drops any config added LATER, silently
# — I nearly removed both files above that way. Enumerating artifacts fails the
# other direction: a new artifact type shows up in `git status`, which is a
# visible problem someone fixes, not an invisible one.
.pmat/context.db
.pmat/context.db-shm
.pmat/context.db-wal
.pmat/context.idx/
.pmat/metrics/
.pmat/*cache*.json
.pv/

# Machine-local build acceleration. NEVER commit this: it pins an ABSOLUTE
# target-dir (/mnt/zram/... on lambda-labs) that does not exist on any other
# machine, so committing it breaks every GitHub-hosted job in the repo with
# "failed to create directory: Permission denied". It reached main via a
# `git add -A` on 2026-08-20 (#9) and took down the nightly binary release for
# all four target platforms.
.cargo/config.toml
